g to try and regulate  and so  we're taking approach of you know  starting low going slow starting out  with uh lower serving sizes but you know  people can include more cannabinoids in  the product uh as long as it's just  transparent and aware for the consumer  and then lastly here uh similar to to  our medical cannabis and adult use  cannabis programs uh we do require  laboratory testing so each lot of a  cannabinoid hemp product uh needs to be  lab tested for a a list of analytes um  and uh is the the consumer should be  able to look up the certificate of  analysis uh for that lab if they ever  want to you know dig deeper and  have some uh reassurance that the the  lot did pass required testing  and so here you can see the uh amount of  licenses that we have issued to date  um  the the retail license really is more of  a registration um so anyone who's  selling can amazon hemp products in new  york state is required to get a a  license from our office to sell these  products  um we're over 3000 now for for retailers  the the application process probably  only takes around 10 minutes there's not  too many questions that that are  required um i think you have to just you  know prove that you have a certificate  of authority list what type of products  you're selling and then the the location  and your website  so it's pretty straightforward where  we're really trying to increase that  number because we do know that there's  likely uh you know four or five thousand  more locations that are selling uh  cannabinoid products just you know  because they are being sold at gas  stations and bodegas and cbd and vape  shops are really uh popping up in a lot  of locations that sell these products  um as you'll see you know we've now  licensed uh over or  just under 50 um  processors so that's really exciting  um  you'll see there's a little bit of a gap  between the number of processor  applications that have been submitted  and then the ones the number that have  been approved um the main reason for  that gap is  just waiting on the applicant to submit  all of their requirements and usually  the gmp audit is the last thing that a  processor will do  so  unlike some of the licenses in the  medical program or the adult use program  our our hemp licenses aren't aren't  competitive i mean if you meet the  requirements of the license you'll  you'll get be able to get the license so  um  the way we have structured the  application is you actually get your  facility you get your gmp audit and then  you can apply and receive that that  final license um so it's not it's not  like a thing where you're you're first  provisionally approved and then you go  find your location and then you write  all your sops it's one of those things  where it's when it's up and running then  it's ready to receive a license  and then uh just quickly on the  distributor permit  that's only required for  uh people who are selling products into  new york state to retailers uh that were  manufactured out of state and that is  just our way to kind of keep track of  the different cannabinoid hemp products  that are being  transported and distributed into new  york state because as we all know there  is a patchwork of laws out there as it  relates to cbd now  a lot of states have kind of followed  the new york model and have their own  specific cannabinoid hemp programs and  they all have different requirements  different testing standards different  packaging and labeling so  it's kind of our way of keeping track of  of you know which products are coming  into the state and trying to make sure  that they meet the requirements of the  new york state program  so uh one uh update here that is kind of  related to the hemp program but not  directly is uh we have started issuing  conditional cultivator licenses on on  the adult use side so uh a bill passed  uh earlier in february of this year that  would essentially that authorized uh  hemp farmers who had grown under the ag  markets program for two of the last four  years uh the opportunity to uh apply for  and receive a license uh to grow the  first adult use cannabis uh that has  been grown legally in new york state in  in uh you know ever  so uh that was really exciting we've  we've launched that application uh the  application actually has since closed um  i think we received over 300 or so  applications we've licensed  223 conditional cultivators um they're  all throughout the state from long  island to western new york to the north  country  um and a lot of different backgrounds  from these these hemp farmers as kind of  tim was alluding to some are you know  experienced farmers who grow 10 other  crops and this is just kind of one more  thing they're adding to their farm  operations  and some are completely new to it  they focusing on cannabis they might  have experience growing  in other locations or their own location  but uh it's been really interesting to  see that program uh roll out and and  it's exciting because uh if we waited  for um all our regulations and for the  licensing system to be up and running we  never would have been able to have uh  you know outdoor grown hemp this year  just because of of new york's climate so  that's really why the conditional  program was so important to get started  and then similarly that same bill that  passed in february also allows for  conditional processors um we're actually  going to be licensing our first batch of  conditional processors at the next  cannabis control board meeting  which is monday so so that'll be  exciting that'll be one more kind of  step in the supply chain to to making  sure that we have we'll be able to get  product uh up and running for when we do  launch the the adult use market  um this conditional processor license is  only available to entities that have a  license uh in the cannabinoid hemp  program and are licensed by the office  and have uh applied for that license  prior to january 1 2022 so that 