 the intoxicating products with the  additional bells and whistles and  regulations would be more appropriately  sold through the adult use in the  medical cannabis markets  um and that leads to the delta athc  which is it's been a big one um just a  quick highlight there that we have  prohibited delta hthc in the cannabinoid  hemp program um it will you know most  likely be allowed in the adult use  program and is also allowed right now in  our medical program  but just because of the intoxicating  nature we're trying to kind of keep  those type of products out of  cannabinoid hemp markets  and then uh farmers markets we get a lot  of questions if can i sell uh  cannabinoid hemp products at a farmers  market the answer is yes  however the uh uh obligation to get a  retail license to do so is is a  requirement um so you know if you have a  retail license already for cannabinoid  hemp products that you sell either  online um just you know bringing that  documentation or having that included  when you set up at a farmer's market  will will count now in terms of a retail  license for for those operations  and then lastly just a quick note um  since legalization i don't know if  anyone's noticed but a lot of these uh  gifting stores have been popping up  since cannabis has been uh you know  decriminalized it's not an enforcement  priority for law enforcement which is a  really good thing however i want to make  it clear that these these these  that our office has not licensed any  adult use sales to date so any of these  stores any of these places selling these  products are not are not legal they're  not authorized by the office they're not  you know their products aren't being  tested there's often labeling concerns  they're often marketed towards kid  children with  you know neon colors and bright stuff so  you know very much please be aware um  when you're when you're  if if you do choose to to you know go to  one of those locations that you don't  really know where these products are  coming from our office is taking a  number of actions trying to uh shut them  down  while we also simultaneously uh  uh licensed products because  these will just you know hurt the the  illicit market that we're trying to to  establish so i kind of just wanted to  highlight that one  um and that that kind of is where we are  right now um you know there's there's a  lot going on  um we're hiring folks uh routinely so  you know if you're interested in a  career or know someone who might be  please check our website there's a jobs  tab where you can see  opportunities for for careers  and  we are looking forward to launching the  adult use program bolstering up the  cannabinoid hemp program and then also  making the medical cannabis program more  accessible for patients and  practitioners  um just a real quick highlight on that  we did recently release  proposed regulations which would  actually get rid of the registration  requirement for our medical program um  so uh  once someone would be just uh  authorized by their physician to to use  medical cannabis they wouldn't have to  then go to our office and get registered  to get registered excuse me uh just  trying to make it easier to essentially  be a medical cannabis patient  in the in the in the light that an adult  use market is coming and we want to make  sure that that medical market exists  because you know sometimes it does make  sense for someone to use cannabis uh  with a practitioner's oversight getting  that feedback you know they might be  taking other medications they might have  questions about dosing and so there's  there's a lot of  pros to to being in the medical program  even in in the existence of an adult  used market  so thank you you know please check out  our website um and uh email us at any of  the many emails that we have  and uh we will try and be as responsive  as possible and i'm open for some  questions if we have time  thanks very much pat uh unfortunately we  are out of time so to ask pat questions  uh so hopefully you snapped a picture of  all of those contacts there  and i'm sure i know they're very busy at  ocm and pat is incredibly busy but  i'm sure they will get back to you  when time allows so  please join me in thanking pat again  with a round of applause  this has been a production of cornell  university on the web at cornell.edu

